# 7. MODEL-CALL TRACE SYSTEM

This is a mandatory judging requirement.

Every model call must be recorded.

Each trace entry must contain:

1. Sequential call number.
2. Actual model name.
3. Area tag.
4. Exact input sent to the model.
5. Exact output received from the model.
6. Input token count reported by the model or provider.
7. Output token count reported by the model or provider.
8. Total tokens for that call.
9. Timestamp.
10. Purpose of the call.

Allowed area tags:

- reading
- venue
- schedule
- food
- judging
- budget

Use one area tag per model call.

Do not invent token counts.

Use actual token usage metadata from the model provider wherever available.

If the provider does not expose token usage, explicitly mark it unavailable instead of fabricating a number.

At the end of the trace, display:

- Total model calls.
- Total input tokens.
- Total output tokens.
- Total tokens.
- Model names used.
- Calls grouped by area.

The trace must be downloadable as a file.

The exact inputs and outputs must be preserved for auditing.

Rejected messages and conflict-resolution explanations must also appear in the trace.

IMPORTANT:

The trace must represent actual model calls, not simulated or manually constructed calls.

Use a centralized model-call wrapper so that no AI call can occur without being logged.

